🎯 COMPREHENSIVE LIKE OPERATOR EXAMPLES WITH _ WILDCARD
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The _ wildcard represents a SINGLE character. Each underscore (_) represents exactly
one, and only one, character. This is more restrictive than % and useful for
fixed-length patterns.

1. PATTERN: WHERE City LIKE '_ondon'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds cities where ANY single character is followed by "ondon"
   MATCHES:
   • 'London' - 'L' matches the underscore
   • 'Condon' - 'C' matches the underscore
   
   DOES NOT MATCH:
   • 'ondon' - Missing the first character
   • 'Londoned' - Has extra characters at the end
   
   QUERY EXAMPLE:
   SELECT * FROM Customers WHERE City LIKE '_ondon';


2. PATTERN: WHERE City LIKE 'L_n_on'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds cities with pattern: L + any char + n + any char + on
   MATCHES:
   • 'London' - L + o + n + d + on ✓
   • 'Lincon' - L + i + n + c + on ✓
   
   DOES NOT MATCH:
   • 'Lanon' - Only 5 characters (needs 6)
   • 'Lanton' - 6 characters but pattern doesn't match
   
   QUERY EXAMPLE:
   SELECT * FROM Customers WHERE City LIKE 'L_n_on';


3. PATTERN: WHERE ProductName LIKE 't__'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds products with names starting with 't' and exactly 3 characters long
   MATCHES:
   • 'tea' - 3 characters starting with 't'
   • 'top' - 3 characters starting with 't'
   • 'toy' - 3 characters starting with 't'
   
   DOES NOT MATCH:
   • 'to' - Only 2 characters
   • 'tent' - 4 characters


4. PATTERN: WHERE Email LIKE '_@%.com'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds emails with pattern: 1 char + @ + any chars + .com
   MATCHES:
   • 'a@example.com' - Starts with single character before @
   • 'b@mail.com' - Starts with single character before @
   
   DOES NOT MATCH:
   • 'ab@example.com' - Has 2 characters before @
   • '@example.com' - Missing the first character


