🎪 COMBINED WILDCARD EXAMPLES (% and _ Together)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. PATTERN: WHERE CustomerName LIKE 'a_%_%'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds values that START with "a" and are AT LEAST 3 characters in length
   EXPLANATION:
   • 'a' - starts with 'a'
   • '_' - any single character
   • '_' - any single character
   • '%' - zero or more characters
   
   MATCHES:
   • 'anna' - a + n + n + a
   • 'antonio' - a + n + t + onio
   • 'alex' - a + l + e + x
   
   DOES NOT MATCH:
   • 'an' - Only 2 characters
   • 'a' - Only 1 character


2. PATTERN: WHERE ProductName LIKE '%c_t%'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds products with pattern: contains c + any char + t anywhere
   MATCHES:
   • 'chocolate' - contains 'cate'
   • 'biscuit' - contains 'cuit'
   • 'scratch' - contains 'cat'
   
   QUERY EXAMPLE:
   SELECT * FROM Products WHERE ProductName LIKE '%c_t%';


3. PATTERN: WHERE Description LIKE '_e%d'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds descriptions that have any char + 'e' at start and end with 'd'
   MATCHES:
   • 'described' - _e%d
   • 'legend' - _e%d
   • 'legend' - _e%d


4. PATTERN: WHERE Address LIKE '%_st%'
   DESCRIPTION: Finds addresses containing any char followed by 'st'
   USE CASE: Finding addresses with "street", "best", "first", etc.


