✨ QUICK REFERENCE GUIDE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Pattern             │ Purpose
────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────
LIKE 'a%'           │ Starts with 'a'
LIKE '%z'           │ Ends with 'z'
LIKE '%or%'         │ Contains 'or' anywhere
LIKE 'a_%_%'        │ Starts with 'a', minimum 3 characters
LIKE '%a%o'         │ Starts with 'a', ends with 'o'
LIKE '_ondon'       │ Any single char followed by 'ondon'
LIKE 'L_n_on'       │ L + any char + n + any char + on
LIKE '_____'        │ Exactly 5 characters
LIKE 'a_b'          │ 3 characters: 'a' + any + 'b'
LIKE '%_st%'        │ Contains any char followed by 'st'

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🎓 SUMMARY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

• % wildcard: Matches ZERO or MORE characters
• _ wildcard: Matches EXACTLY ONE character
• LIKE is case-INSENSITIVE by default
• Use with WHERE clause for pattern matching
• Combine wildcards for complex patterns
• Avoid leading % for better performance
• Remember that NULL does NOT match wildcards
• Use ESCAPE clause to search for literal % or _

